spec ww04-update-delete-commit: 2 sessions, 6 permutations
# WW04, commit arm. s1 updates node n, s2 DETACH DELETEs it; both commit. Whichever
# writes second is refused, while the first is open and after it commits (the head
# is not visible to the later snapshot). Both orders are enumerated.

starting permutation: s1u s1c s2d s2c
step s1u: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) SET n.x = 1 RETURN n.x AS x
x
-
1
(1 row)
step s1c: COMMIT
step s2d: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) DETACH DELETE n RETURN count(*) AS deleted
deleted
